hailo_v2_compile_report.txt
# Compiled HEFs plus the exporter's metadata.yaml / nms_config.json sidecars.
# *.hef is already ignored globally; these two sidecars are not, and the kit
# rule above puts model artefacts outside git with a tracked pointer in
# models/current/README.md. The baked conf/iou end up in the compile report.
models/current/hef_v2/

hailo_dataflow_compiler-3.34.0-py3-none-linux_x86_64.whl

docs/HANDOFF*

# Run archives pulled back off the network volume: a full runs/detect/<run>/
# directory, periodic epoch checkpoints included. 179 MB and 640 MB respectively,
# both far over GitHub's 100 MB push limit.
#
# These two lines previously read ".tar" with no suffix, which matched NOTHING --
# the files on disk are ".tar.gz", so 819 MB sat untracked-but-not-ignored and
# turned up in every `git status`. The trailing glob now covers .tar, .tar.gz and
# any future .tar.zst, matching the dataset/bundle.tar.* rule above.
#
# Both are reproducible: the run directories live on the EU-RO-1 network volume
# under /workspace/model_backups/, and their sha256 was verified identical to
# these local copies (DEC-142).
cap4500_yolov8s_v2_20260913T164555Z.tar*

cap4500_yolov8s_v2-2_20260913T164555Z.tar*

# Label/list tarballs staged for upload to the pod, written by
# scripts/train/stage_v3_arms.py. Already covered by the blanket `dataset/` rule
# above; named explicitly so the intent survives if that rule is ever narrowed.
dataset/staging/

